    "turn_text": "Hello, and welcome to American Exchange with me, Eric McElroy, where I, as an American expat living in the UK, dial back overseas and try and connect with what is happening in the United States. This is our tenth episode, which is, I think, exciting. I hope you think it's exciting as well. And since it is special, we brought back our very first guest, Joe Walsh. because he's in the heartland of America. If you haven't heard of Joe before, he's a former congressman. He was a Tea Party Republican. He has got a national talk show in the US. And he's come out against Trump in 2018, basically, because he just couldn't take it anymore. Couldn't take the lies, couldn't take what Trump was doing to our democracy. And he spent the last two years doing everything he could to help make Trump a one-term president. What's incredible is because he has turned away from the Republican Party in such an open way It gives him the freedom to be very very candid so he can criticize his former colleagues But then he can also openly praise the people that he used to be against on the other side of the aisle Which is a great way. He's not guarded anymore in any way whatsoever So, incredible insights, what's happening in the state of play, now that Trump has lost, what we can expect over the next month, which could be kind of",
