    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51104.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "I suppose that's a good thing because the two parties haven't served all of their constituents very effectively and that's why they've had the problems that they've had. But I've watched here with the, you know, the Tories, I can't remember the numbers, but you know, they have a huge majority in the parliament here, but they only won 43 or 45% of the national vote. And, you know, it's drawn us into Brexit and other things. So it's not, we're being, you know, we're being led by a minority party.",
