    "turn_idx": 135,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. You know, look, I think you and I have talked about this. How did Trump so easily take over the Republican Party? Because You have a bunch of older white people in America, the Republican base, who had been crying out for years to their party, listened to us. We're angry and we're scared. I got people coming into my country illegally. I got my plant leaving my country. I've got an opioid crisis. I've got, I'm now told there are 64 different genders in America. Listen to me, this is craziness. And the party ignored them. So finally, along comes a demagogue four years, five years ago. And he says, I hear you. I'm going to build a fucking wall and I'll make Mexico pay for it. Done. He had them. He was the first Republican. It was all alive. But the first Republican who said, I hear you, you're angry and scared. I hear you. I'll do something about it.",
