    "turn_idx": 273,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think what's happened to the Republican Party and what Joe now has come back to because he was on the extreme of the the Tea Party, and he said some stuff back in the day about Obama that he admits now was inappropriate, and he's apologized for. But because he's now left the party in a way, he can be more what a true quote unquote conservative Republican is supposed to be, which is what he talks about being a small government person who allows freedom of choice and that sense to come forward. But he can only be that way now because it's not because Trump's Republican Party isn't that. Trump's Republican Party is Trump. And what I also like about talking to somebody who's now kind of left the system and gone their own way is that he can be critical of his own party, and he can also be complementary to the opposition party, which is something in America you can't do right now normally. If you're still in the game, you can't admit that Nancy Pelosi is strategically brilliant. She's the enemy. And that level of rhetoric and that level of, that's why people now believe that Joe Biden is going to undermine America and everything else because it's just been taken to such an extreme, which I don't think we have achieved here in the UK yet. I don't think anybody thinks that the other team is an enemy of the country, really. I don't know, I'm trying to think if that holds true.",
