    "turn_idx": 313,
    "turn_text": "there's got to be a little bit of accountability there. But yeah, I think we've got a couple, we've got some rocky weeks coming ahead. Joe Biden will be inaugurated on the 20th. And then I think Joe's right, there is going to be semi calming, because you just can't, Joe's not going to be the character that winds everybody up. He's not going to be in your face every day. There are going to be days where we forget who the president is. And that is going to be a blessed moment. Well, there you have it, guys. That was Joe Walsh. Thank you very much to Joe for coming back on the show. Thank you, as always, for Mark, the producer, for putting everything together for us and giving us that British perspective. Make sure to check out Joe's podcast, Fox Silence. It's a great name, although they do it with the asterisk. So fuck asterisk. And so on, follow him on Twitter at Walsh Freedom. And please subscribe to this podcast. Please let people know if you enjoy it. Give us a rating if you can. We're 10 episodes in. We've had some incredible guests. Go back and listen to Mary Trump, Anthony Scaramucci, Olivia Troy, who used to work in the Trump administration. And yeah, please keep supporting the podcast. And we will see you next time. Thanks very much for listening. Bye bye.",
